<!--
  CLion CMake profiles for this ESP-IDF project.

  IMPORTANT: building on the host is NOT supported. All builds run inside the
  ESP-IDF dev container (ESP-IDF v6.1). Each subproject's CMakeLists.txt
  enforces this by requiring the /etc/esp32-sensors-dev-container marker,
  which the Dockerfile creates and docker-compose.yml mounts.

  CLion reaches the container through the Dev Container defined in
  .devcontainer/devcontainer.json, which reuses the `dev` service from
  docker-compose.yml. CMake, Ninja, and the Xtensa/Linux toolchains therefore
  run in the container.

  FILE FORMAT
  ===========
  CLion stores these profiles through CMakeSharedSettingsStorage, whose XML
  state is the element *children* of <component name="CMakeSharedSettings">.
  It reads `configurations` -> `configuration` and understands only these
  attributes:
      PROFILE_NAME, ENABLED, CONFIG_NAME, TOOLCHAIN_NAME,
      GENERATION_DIR, BUILD_OPTIONS, GENERATION_OPTIONS,
      GENERATION_PASS_SYSTEM_ENVIRONMENT, ADDITIONAL_GENERATION_ENVIRONMENT,
      NO_GENERATOR, FROM_PRESET

  Do NOT use the pre-2023 shape (`<option name="configurations"><list>` with
  BUILD_DIR / CMAKE_OPTIONS / GENERATOR_NAME): the current loader finds no
  `configurations` child there, so the project ends up with ZERO CMake
  profiles and the CMake run configuration fails with "cannot find any
  profile". Edit the profile in Settings | Build, Execution, Deployment |
  CMake, or update the attributes above - never reintroduce the old names.
  In particular a profile has NO "generation directory" of the *source*
  project - it has no way to point CMake at a subdirectory. See the KNOWN
  LIMITATION at the end of this comment for what that means in practice: the
  profiles are meant to be one per subproject, but today every one of them
  configures the repo root instead.

  ONE PROFILE PER EXECUTABLE
  ==========================
  The repo root is NOT an ESP-IDF project: its CMakeLists.txt is a plain
  aggregator, `project(... NONE)`, that only defines custom targets which
  shell out to `idf.py`. Each subproject, on the other hand, is a standalone
  ESP-IDF project and ESP-IDF turns on CMAKE_EXPORT_COMPILE_COMMANDS by
  default, so configuring it emits a compile_commands.json that CLion turns
  into a full resolve configuration. Hence one profile per subproject, keyed
  by profile name to its ELF run configuration in .idea/runConfigurations/:

      profile                       subproject
      Espressif ESP32-S3            mcgowan/
      Host tests (test-utility)     components/utility/tests/test-utility/
      Host tests (test-hal-stub)    components/hal/tests/test-hal-stub/
      Host tests (test-hal-common)  components/hal/tests/test-hal-common/
      Host tests (test-logic)       components/logic/tests/test-logic/
      Host tests (test-espidf-cpp)  components/espidfcpp/tests/test-espidf-cpp/
      Host tests (test-simulator)   components/simulator/tests/test-simulator/
      Host tests (esp_timer stub)   components/hal/tests/esp_timer/stub/
      Linux app (donny)             components/simulator/exe/donny/

  The `<name> (linux ELF, container)` configurations build through the
  matching `<sub>_build` root target and run the generated ELF. Debug works
  because the host tests are compiled with `-gdwarf-4 -ggdb -Og`, and the
  CLion backend runs inside the same container as the ELF.

  BUILD DIRECTORIES
  =================
  Each profile keeps its OWN build tree, named cmake-build-*, so CLion never
  shares a CMake cache with the canonical `idf.py` trees that
  `scripts/dev.py` writes (e.g. mcgowan/build_esp32s3,
  components/logic/tests/test-logic/build_linux). Sharing a directory does
  not work: idf.py and CLion overwrite each other's CMake cache and Ninja
  state. All cmake-build-* directories are git-ignored (`.gitignore`).

  COEXISTING RESOLVE CONFIGURATIONS
  =================================
  The projects share sources - mcgowan/src is compiled by several linux
  suites, and components/* by all of them - and mcgowan (Xtensa, esp32s3)
  and the others (host, linux) genuinely need different defines and include
  paths, notably which of hal_board / hal_stub is in view. CLion keeps each
  profile's resolve configuration separate and switches with the active
  profile (the run configuration's CONFIG_NAME), which is why every profile
  must be kept, not merged.

  TOOLCHAIN_NAME is the Dev Container toolchain ("Default", the system
  toolset inside the container); the generator is left unspecified so CLion
  uses Ninja. GENERATION_OPTIONS also pins -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Debug so the
  compile database carries debug info and CLion's default CONFIG_NAME=Debug
  matches a configuration that actually exists.

  KNOWN LIMITATION: the profiles above do NOT actually configure their
  subproject yet, so the code model they were meant to provide does not
  exist. GENERATION_DIR is only the *build* directory; the *source* directory
  comes from the single CMake workspace, .idea/misc.xml
  (CMakeWorkspace PROJECT_DIR="$PROJECT_DIR$"), which is the repo root for
  every profile. Observed after a clean CLion rebuild: all cmake-build-*
  trees record CMAKE_HOME_DIRECTORY=/project, none contains a
  compile_commands.json, each one's codemodel names project
  `esp32_sensors_subprojects`, and the only targets are the aggregate
  custom targets - all of type UTILITY, i.e. no compilable translation units.
  A profile has no per-profile source directory. Code model, navigation and
  tooltips come instead from `scripts/dev.py clion-compdb`, which merges the
  subprojects' compile databases into .clion/compile_commands.json for CLion
  to open as a compilation-database project (see AGENTS.md). Until then,
  navigation and refactorings are not driven by these profiles; the ELF run
  configurations still work because their executable path is given explicitly.
-->
<project version="4">
  <component name="CMakeSharedSettings">
    <configurations>
      <configuration PROFILE_NAME="Espressif ESP32-S3" ENABLED="true" CONFIG_NAME="Debug" TOOLCHAIN_NAME="Default" GENERATION_DIR="$PROJECT_DIR$/mcgowan/cmake-build-esp32s3" GENERATION_OPTIONS="-DIDF_TARGET=esp32s3 -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Debug" />
      <configuration PROFILE_NAME="Host tests (test-utility)" ENABLED="true" CONFIG_NAME="Debug" TOOLCHAIN_NAME="Default" GENERATION_DIR="$PROJECT_DIR$/components/utility/tests/test-utility/cmake-build-linux-test-utility" GENERATION_OPTIONS="-DIDF_TARGET=linux -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Debug" />
      <configuration PROFILE_NAME="Host tests (test-hal-stub)" ENABLED="true" CONFIG_NAME="Debug" TOOLCHAIN_NAME="Default" GENERATION_DIR="$PROJECT_DIR$/components/hal/tests/test-hal-stub/cmake-build-linux-test-hal-stub" GENERATION_OPTIONS="-DIDF_TARGET=linux -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Debug" />
      <configuration PROFILE_NAME="Host tests (test-hal-common)" ENABLED="true" CONFIG_NAME="Debug" TOOLCHAIN_NAME="Default" GENERATION_DIR="$PROJECT_DIR$/components/hal/tests/test-hal-common/cmake-build-linux-test-hal-common" GENERATION_OPTIONS="-DIDF_TARGET=linux -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Debug" />
      <configuration PROFILE_NAME="Host tests (test-logic)" ENABLED="true" CONFIG_NAME="Debug" TOOLCHAIN_NAME="Default" GENERATION_DIR="$PROJECT_DIR$/components/logic/tests/test-logic/cmake-build-linux-test-logic" GENERATION_OPTIONS="-DIDF_TARGET=linux -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Debug" />
      <configuration PROFILE_NAME="Host tests (test-espidf-cpp)" ENABLED="true" CONFIG_NAME="Debug" TOOLCHAIN_NAME="Default" GENERATION_DIR="$PROJECT_DIR$/components/espidfcpp/tests/test-espidf-cpp/cmake-build-linux-test-espidf-cpp" GENERATION_OPTIONS="-DIDF_TARGET=linux -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Debug" />
      <configuration PROFILE_NAME="Host tests (test-simulator)" ENABLED="true" CONFIG_NAME="Debug" TOOLCHAIN_NAME="Default" GENERATION_DIR="$PROJECT_DIR$/components/simulator/tests/test-simulator/cmake-build-linux-test-simulator" GENERATION_OPTIONS="-DIDF_TARGET=linux -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Debug" />
      <configuration PROFILE_NAME="Host tests (esp_timer stub)" ENABLED="true" CONFIG_NAME="Debug" TOOLCHAIN_NAME="Default" GENERATION_DIR="$PROJECT_DIR$/components/hal/tests/esp_timer/stub/cmake-build-linux-esp-timer-stub" GENERATION_OPTIONS="-DIDF_TARGET=linux -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Debug" />
      <configuration PROFILE_NAME="Linux app (donny)" ENABLED="true" CONFIG_NAME="Debug" TOOLCHAIN_NAME="Default" GENERATION_DIR="$PROJECT_DIR$/components/simulator/exe/donny/cmake-build-linux-donny" GENERATION_OPTIONS="-DIDF_TARGET=linux -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Debug" />
    </configurations>
  </component>
</project>
